# snapback configuration — example
#
# Copy the section you need to the right place and edit it:
#
#   project-local:  <project>/.snapshotrc      (created by: snapback init --local)
#   global:         ~/.snapshotrc              (created by: snapback sampleconfig > ~/.snapshotrc)
#
# snapback reads, in order of priority:
#   1. ./.snapshotrc in the current directory (project-local mode)
#   2. an explicit --config PATH, or $SNAPSHOTRC
#   3. ~/.snapshotrc (global mode)
#
# Values may be quoted with ' or ". Quote any value containing spaces: the file is
# read like shell assignments, and an unquoted space-separated list breaks it.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROJECT-LOCAL (recommended for repositories and agent workflows)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Snapshots live inside the project, so a rollback needs no global state and each
# project keeps its own history. Create it with:
#
#   cd /path/to/project
#   snapback init --local                      # snapshots in ./.snapshots
#   snapback init --local --snapshots-dir .snapback   # or any directory you prefer
#
# init writes this file, creates the snapshot directory and adds both the snapshot
# directory and .snapshotrc to .gitignore.

# Directories to back up. '.' means the whole project.
DIRS='.'

# Where snapshots are stored. Must stay inside the project. Use the same directory
# you passed to --snapshots-dir. This directory is excluded from its own snapshots,
# so pointing it somewhere else never makes snapshots of snapshots.
TARGETBASE='./.snapback'

# Optional extra rsync parameters. Keep them quoted.
# Examples:
#   --max-size=10m          skip files larger than 10MB
#   --exclude=*.pyc         skip Python bytecode
#   --exclude=build/        skip a build directory
RSYNC_PARAMS=''

# Retention defaults (only set these if you need different rotation):
# H_SNAPS=23      hourly snapshots kept
# D_SNAPS=7       daily snapshots kept
# W_SNAPS=4       weekly snapshots kept
# M_SNAPS=12      monthly snapshots kept


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GLOBAL (traditional: snapshots outside the project, absolute paths required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DIRS='/home/you/Documents /home/you/Projects'
# TARGETBASE='/home/you/.Snapshots'
# RSYNC_PARAMS=''
#
# Global mode accepts absolute paths only, and it does not apply .gitignore
# filtering: everything under DIRS is copied.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Restoring — read this before your first rollback
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# snapback recover <snapshot>     full rollback: restores the snapshot over the
#                                 project, deleting files added since (protected
#                                 paths below are never touched)
#   --dry-run                     show what would change, change nothing
#   --keep-existing               restore only what is missing; never delete or
#                                 overwrite — the safe choice when unsure
#
# snapback undel <snapshot>       restore deleted files only; never deletes
#
# Paths that snapshots never contain are protected from deletion: .git, gitignored
# files and directories, the snapshot directory itself, and this config file.
#
# Verify a rollback before trusting it: after recovering, check that .git still
# exists and that your gitignored content is still there.
